 "structural_change": "S81-ELEM2-HWIN successor of dsdv_mu_hwin_c21q (daemon NEEDS_RTL: c21q TT -148.19 / FF -8.26, c21r TT -141.73 / FF -11.76, DRC 0). Failing class: g_compare_copy.cmp_r -> 47-entry identity compare + OR reduce -> global duplicate flag udup -> distributed to all 16x2 event rec_r + slot record_group across the 561.6 um band (two 113/148 ps buffer hops, arrival 1222.75 vs required 1081.02). Fix (RTL, codex adf49d4f8 LOCAL_RECORD=1): each of the (NEV/4 event + 6 slot) record consumer groups gets its own kept duplicate-region cone (2 local 10-bit user landing flops, 47 compares, 8-entry partial ORs), so admission drives <= 8 local record flops instead of a band-wide broadcast; 0 cycles added (waveform miter vs frozen HWIN21cb + anchor). NEV 8 = the exact G8IQ die parameter (dsdv_seq_host_mux u_hwin), 44 SRAMs, outline 345.6 x 388.8 (band 341 um wide instead of 557: every cone/band hop shorter). Physical: c21j hash-locked native manifests/fences dropped (cannot qualify changed RTL); c21h row-pruned band + GPL row envelope instead; pd 0.48; OPT_POST_GRT_WNS=0 pre_grt kept (EST-0104 class).",
